      "index": 0,
      "text": "421, 110.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **978** and **435**, we'll use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0} \\ 978 \\\\\n\\times \\ 435 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 978 by 5 (the units digit of 435)\n\\[\n978 \\times 5 = 4,890\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 978 by 30 (the tens digit of 435, shifted one position to the left)\n\\[\n978 \\times 30 = 29,340\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 978 by 400 (the hundreds digit of 435, shifted two positions to the left)\n\\[\n978 \\times 400 = 391,200\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add all the partial products together\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{00}4,890 \\\\\n+ \\phantom{0}29,340 \\\\\n+ 391,200 \\\\\n\\hline\n421,110 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{421,\\!110}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
