      "text": "91,700 + 5,240 + 262 = 97,202.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **131** and **742**, we'll use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}131 \\\\\n\\times\\phantom{0}742 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Step 1:** Multiply 131 by 2 (the units digit of 742).\n\n\\[\n131 \\times 2 = 262\n\\]\n\n**Step 2:** Multiply 131 by 40 (the tens digit of 742, shifted one position to the left).\n\n\\[\n131 \\times 40 = 5,240\n\\]\n\n**Step 3:** Multiply 131 by 700 (the hundreds digit of 742, shifted two positions to the left).\n\n\\[\n131 \\times 700 = 91,700\n\\]\n\n**Step 4:** Add all the results together.\n\n\\[\n262 + 5,240 + 91,700 = 97,202\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{97,\\!202}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
