      "index": 0,
      "text": "226,646.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **418** and **547**, we'll use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}418 \\\\\n\\times\\phantom{0}547 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 418 by 7 (ones place of 547)\n\\[\n418 \\times 7 = 2926\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 418 by 40 (tens place of 547)\n\\[\n418 \\times 40 = 16720\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 418 by 500 (hundreds place of 547)\n\\[\n418 \\times 500 = 209000\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add all the partial products together\n\\[\n2926 + 16720 + 209000 = 226646\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{226646}\n\\]",
