      "index": 0,
      "text": "109,600 + 10,960 + 4,932 = 125,492.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **548** and **229**, we'll use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}548 \\\\\n\\times\\phantom{0}229 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\phantom{0}548 \\times 9 = 4,932 \\\\\n\\phantom{0}548 \\times 20 = 10,960 \\\\\n\\phantom{0}548 \\times 200 = 109,600 \\\\\n\\hline\n125,492 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 548 by 9:**\n   \\[\n   548 \\times 9 = 4,932\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply 548 by 20:**\n   \\[\n   548 \\times 20 = 10,960\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply 548 by 200:**\n   \\[\n   548 \\times 200 = 109,600\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   4,932 + 10,960 + 109,600 = 125,492\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{125,\\!492}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
