  "id": "cmpl-a91647b3cfe1470c8f42265b3160d276",
  "object": "text_completion",
  "created": 1754579626,
  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-7B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "113,200 plus 7,924, which equals 121,124.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **566** and **214**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, decompose **214** into **200** and **14** for easier multiplication.\n\n\\[\n214 = 200 + 14\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 566 by 200\n\\[\n566 \\times 200 = 113,\\!200\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 566 by 14\nBreak down **14** into **10** and **4**:\n\n\\[\n566 \\times 14 = 566 \\times (10 + 4) = (566 \\times 10) + (566 \\times 4)\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part:\n\n\\[\n566 \\times 10 = 5,\\!660\n\\]\n\\[\n566 \\times 4 = 2,\\!264\n\\]\n\nAdd them together:\n\n\\[\n5,\\!660 + 2,\\!264 = 7,\\!924\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add the Results\nNow, add the results from Step 2 and Step 3:\n\n\\[\n113,\\!200 + 7,\\!924 = 121,\\!124\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{121,\\!124}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
