messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 736 and 698?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 736 and 698, I'll start by breaking down each number into smaller, more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll express 736 as 700 plus 36, and 698 as 700 minus 2. This allows me to use the difference of squares formula, which states that (a + b)(a - b) equals a squared minus b squared.\n\nApplying this formula, I'll square 700 and then square 2. Subtracting the square of 2 from the square of 700 will give me the final product of 736 and 698.\n. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
response:  {
  "id": "cmpl-f38e4ca8a07a4d009783716d3e61503f",
  "object": "text_completion",
  "created": 1754579679,
  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-7B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "514,648.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **736** and **698**, we'll use the **distributive property** (also known as the **FOIL method**) for multiplying two binomials. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n736 \\times 698 &= (700 + 36) \\times (700 - 2) \\\\\n&= 700 \\times 700 - 700 \\times 2 + 36 \\times 700 - 36 \\times 2 \\\\\n&= 490,\\!000 - 1,\\!400 + 25,\\!200 - 72 \\\\\n&= 490,\\!000 - 1,\\!400 = 488,\\!600 \\\\\n488,\\!600 + 25,\\!200 &= 513,\\!800 \\\\\n513,\\!800 - 72 &= 514,\\!648 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{514,\\!648}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
