      "text": "351,  6  0  8.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **628** and **561**, we'll use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}628 \\\\\n\\times\\phantom{0}561 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 628 by 1 (units place)\n\\[\n628 \\times 1 = 628\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 628 by 60 (tens place)\n\\[\n628 \\times 60 = 37,680\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 628 by 500 (hundreds place)\n\\[\n628 \\times 500 = 314,000\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add all the results together\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}628 \\\\\n+37,680 \\\\\n+314,000 \\\\\n\\hline\n351,608 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{351,\\!608}\n\\]",
