messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 104 and 294?', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 104 and 294, I'll start by breaking down 294 into 200 and 94. This makes the multiplication easier to handle.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 104 by 200. Multiplying by 200 is the same as multiplying by 2 and then adding two zeros at the end. So, 104 times 2 is 208, and adding two zeros gives me 20,800.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 104 by 94. To simplify this, I'll break down 94 into 90 and 4. .\n\nFirst, I'll calculate 104 times 90. Multiplying 104 by 9 gives 936, and adding a zero gives me 9,360.\n\nThen, I'll calculate 104 times 4, which is 416.\n\nFinally, I'll add the two results together: 9,360 plus 416 equals 9,776. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
