      "text": "34,000 + 20,400 + 2,040 = 56,440.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **340** and **166**, follow these easy steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nUse the distributive property to simplify the multiplication:\n\\[\n340 \\times 166 = 340 \\times (100 + 60 + 6)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\n1. **Multiply by 100:**\n\\[\n340 \\times 100 = 34,\\!000\n\\]\n2. **Multiply by 60:**\n\\[\n340 \\times 60 = 20,\\!400\n\\]\n3. **Multiply by 6:**\n\\[\n340 \\times 6 = 2,\\!040\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Results Together\n\\[\n34,\\!000 + 20,\\!400 + 2,\\!040 = 56,\\!440\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{56,\\!440}\n\\]",
