messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 761 and 526?', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 761 and 526, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 761 by 500. This is straightforward since multiplying by 500 is the same as multiplying by 5 and then by 100. So, 761 times 5 equals 3,805, and then multiplying by 100 gives me 380,500.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 761 by 26. To make this easier, I'll break it down further into 761 times 20 and 761 times 6. .\n\nMultiplying 761 by 20 gives me 15,220, and multiplying 761 by 6 results in 4,566. Adding these two amounts together, 15,220 plus 4,566 equals 19,786.\n\nFinally, I'll add the two main parts together: 380,500 plus 19,786. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
