messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 414 and 142?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 414 and 142, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 414 by 100, which gives me 41,400.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 414 by 40, resulting in 16,560.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 414 by 2, which equals 828.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 41,400 plus 16,560 plus 828 to get the final result.\n. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
response:  {
  "id": "cmpl-8b00c02926234dd4b1eb8d6e850c150b",
  "object": "text_completion",
  "created": 1754580323,
  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-7B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "58,788.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **414** and **142**, we'll use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n414 \\times 142 &= 414 \\times (100 + 40 + 2) \\\\\n&= 414 \\times 100 + 414 \\times 40 + 414 \\times 2 \\\\\n&= 41,\\!400 + 16,\\!560 + 828 \\\\\n&= 41,\\!400 + 16,\\!560 \\\\\n&= 57,\\!960 \\\\\n&\\quad + \\,\\, 828 \\\\\n&= 58,\\!788\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{58,\\!788}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
  ],
