      "index": 0,
      "text": "499 \u00d7 543 = 270,957.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **499** and **543**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nStart by expressing **499** as **500 - 1** to simplify the multiplication.\n\n\\[\n499 \\times 543 = (500 - 1) \\times 543\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Apply the Distributive Property\nMultiply **543** by both **500** and **-1**.\n\n\\[\n(500 \\times 543) - (1 \\times 543)\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **Multiply 500 by 543:**\n   \n   \\[\n   500 \\times 543 = 271,500\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply 1 by 543:**\n   \n   \\[\n   1 \\times 543 = 543\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Subtract the Two Results\n\n\\[\n271,500 - 543 = 270,957\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{270,\\!957}\n\\]",
