messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 218 and 561?', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 218 and 561, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 218 by 500, which is straightforward since multiplying by 100s is simple. 218 multiplied by 500 equals 109,000.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 218 by 60. This can be done by multiplying 218 by 6 and then adding a zero at the end. 218 times 6 is 1,308, so adding a zero gives me 13,080.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 218 by 1, which is just 218.\n\nNow, I'll add all these results together: 109,000 plus 13,080 plus 218. Adding 109,000 and 13,080 gives me 122,080. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
