      "text": "215,296.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **928** and **232**, we'll use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}928 \\\\\n\\times\\phantom{0}232 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 928 by 2 (units place of 232)\n\\[\n928 \\times 2 = 1,\\!856\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 928 by 30 (tens place of 232)\n\\[\n928 \\times 30 = 27,\\!840\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 928 by 200 (hundreds place of 232)\n\\[\n928 \\times 200 = 185,\\!600\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add all the partial products together\n\\[\n1,\\!856 + 27,\\!840 + 185,\\!600 = 215,\\!296\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{215,\\!296}\n\\]",
