  "id": "cmpl-44c2b8ab627b4ed9a91e44aa7e0ce2ac",
  "object": "text_completion",
  "created": 1754581070,
  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-7B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "425,103.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **651** and **653**, we can use the **difference of squares** formula, which simplifies the multiplication process. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n651 \\times 653 = (652 - 1) \\times (652 + 1)\n\\]\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula:\n\n\\[\n(a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\n\\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( a = 652 \\)\n- \\( b = 1 \\)\n\n\\[\n651 \\times 653 = 652^2 - 1^2\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate \\( 652^2 \\):\n\n\\[\n652^2 = 652 \\times 652 = 425,\\!104\n\\]\n\nAnd \\( 1^2 = 1 \\).\n\nSubtracting the two results:\n\n\\[\n425,\\!104 - 1 = 425,\\!103\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{425,\\!103}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
