      "text": "851 multiplied by 816 equals 692,  616.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **851** and **816**, we'll use the **distributive property** (also known as the **FOIL method** for binomials) to simplify the multiplication. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n851 \\times 816 &= (800 + 50 + 1) \\times (800 + 16) \\\\\n&= 800 \\times 800 + 800 \\times 16 + 50 \\times 800 + 50 \\times 16 + 1 \\times 800 + 1 \\times 16 \\\\\n&= 640,\\!000 + 12,\\!800 + 40,\\!000 + 800 + 800 + 16 \\\\\n&= 640,\\!000 + 12,\\!800 = 652,\\!800 \\\\\n652,\\!800 + 40,\\!000 &= 692,\\!800 \\\\\n692,\\!800 + 800 &= 693,\\!600 \\\\\n693,\\!600 + 800 &= 694,\\!400 \\\\\n694,\\!400 + 16 &= 694,\\!416 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{694,\\!416}\n\\]",
