  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-7B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "280,000.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **560** and **500**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Numbers:**\n   \n   \\[\n   560 \\times 500 = (500 + 60) \\times 500\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply Each Part Separately:**\n   \n   - Multiply **500** by **500**:\n     \n     \\[\n     500 \\times 500 = 250,\\!000\n     \\]\n   \n   - Multiply **500** by **60**:\n     \n     \\[\n     500 \\times 60 = 30,\\!000\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add the Results Together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   250,\\!000 + 30,\\!000 = 280,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{280,\\!000}\n   \\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
