      "text": "334, 104.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **684** and **486**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, let's break down the numbers into their place values:\n\n\\[\n684 = 600 + 80 + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n486 = 400 + 80 + 6\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nNow, multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n600 \\times 400 &= 240,\\!000 \\\\\n600 \\times 80 &= 48,\\!000 \\\\\n600 \\times 6 &= 3,\\!600 \\\\\n80 \\times 400 &= 32,\\!000 \\\\\n80 \\times 80 &= 6,\\!400 \\\\\n80 \\times 6 &= 480 \\\\\n4 \\times 400 &= 1,\\!600 \\\\\n4 \\times 80 &= 320 \\\\\n4 \\times 6 &= 24 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nNow, sum all the individual products:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n240,\\!000 &+ 48,\\!000 + 3,\\!600 \\\\\n&+ 32,\\!000 + 6,\\!400 + 480 \\\\\n&+ 1,\\!600 + 320 + 24 \\\\\n&= 334,\\!104 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{334,\\!104}\n\\]",
