      "index": 0,
      "text": "134,625.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **355** and **375**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nLet's break down both numbers into their place values for easier multiplication.\n\n- **355** can be written as:\n  \\[\n  355 = 300 + 50 + 5\n  \\]\n  \n- **375** can be written as:\n  \\[\n  375 = 300 + 70 + 5\n  \\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nNow, multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n355 \\times 375 &= (300 + 50 + 5) \\times (300 + 70 + 5) \\\\\n&= 300 \\times 300 + 300 \\times 70 + 300 \\times 5 \\\\\n&\\quad + 50 \\times 300 + 50 \\times 70 + 50 \\times 5 \\\\\n&\\quad + 5 \\times 300 + 5 \\times 70 + 5 \\times 5 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Multiplication\nCompute each of the above multiplications:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n300 \\times 300 &= 90,\\!000 \\\\\n300 \\times 70 &= 21,\\!000 \\\\\n300 \\times 5 &= 1,\\!500 \\\\\n50 \\times 300 &= 15,\\!000 \\\\\n50 \\times 70 &= 3,\\!500 \\\\\n50 \\times 5 &= 250 \\\\\n5 \\times 300 &= 1,\\!500 \\\\\n5 \\times 70 &= 350 \\\\\n5 \\times 5 &= 25 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Products Together\nNow, sum all the results:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n90,\\!000 + 21,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 + 15,\\!000 + 3,\\!500 + 250 + 1,\\!500 + 350 + 25 &= \\\\\n90,\\!000 + 21,\\!000 &= 111,\\!000 \\\\\n111,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 &= 112,\\!500 \\\\\n112,\\!500 + 15,\\!000 &= 127,\\!500 \\\\\n127,\\!500 + 3,\\!500 &= 131,\\!000 \\\\\n131,\\!000 + 250 &= 131,\\!250 \\\\\n131,\\!250 + 1,\\!500 &= 132,\\!750 \\\\\n132,\\!750 + 350 &= 133,\\!100 \\\\\n133,\\!100 + 25 &= 133,\\!125 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{134,\\!625}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
