      "text": "937, 136.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **947** and **988**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can express **988** as **1000 - 12** to simplify the multiplication.\n\n\\[\n947 \\times 988 = 947 \\times (1000 - 12)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Apply the Distributive Property\nMultiply **947** by each part separately.\n\n\\[\n947 \\times 1000 = 947,000\n\\]\n\\[\n947 \\times 12 = 11,364\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Subtract the Results\nNow, subtract the second product from the first.\n\n\\[\n947,000 - 11,364 = 935,636\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{935,\\!636}\n\\]",
