      "text": "90,800 + 36,320 = 127,120.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **908** and **140**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   908 \\times 140 = 908 \\times (100 + 40)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 908 by 100:**\n\n   \\[\n   908 \\times 100 = 90,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 908 by 40:**\n\n   \\[\n   908 \\times 40 = 36,\\!320\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the Two Results Together:**\n\n   \\[\n   90,\\!800 + 36,\\!320 = 127,\\!120\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{127,\\!120}\n   \\]",
