messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 446 and 448?', '<think>.\nTo find the product of 446 and 448, I can use the difference of squares formula.\n\nFirst, I notice that 446 and 448 are two numbers that are 2 units apart. I can express them as (447 - 1) and (447 + 1), respectively.\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula, (a - b)(a + b) equals a squared minus b squared.\n\nHere, a is 447 and b is 1. So, the product becomes 447 squared minus 1 squared. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
response:  {
  "id": "cmpl-4b2320b9ea5d461ebc593eb048c05839",
  "object": "text_completion",
  "created": 1754582217,
  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-7B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "447\u00b2 - 1.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **446** and **448**, we can use the **difference of squares** formula. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n446 \\times 448 = (447 - 1) \\times (447 + 1)\n\\]\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula:\n\n\\[\n(a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\n\\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( a = 447 \\)\n- \\( b = 1 \\)\n\n\\[\n446 \\times 448 = 447^2 - 1^2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n446 \\times 448 = 447^2 - 1\n\\]\n\nSo, the product of **446** and **448** is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{447^2 - 1}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
