  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "58,500 + 7,020 + 351 = 65,871.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **117** and **563**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nUse the distributive property to simplify the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n117 \\times 563 = 117 \\times (500 + 60 + 3)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part Separately\n\n1. **Multiply by 500:**\n   \\[\n   117 \\times 500 = 58,\\!500\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by 60:**\n   \\[\n   117 \\times 60 = 7,\\!020\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by 3:**\n   \\[\n   117 \\times 3 = 351\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Results Together\n\n\\[\n58,\\!500 + 7,\\!020 + 351 = 65,\\!871\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{65,\\!871}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
