      "index": 0,
      "text": "207,  618.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **651** and **318**, we'll use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 651 by 300\n\\[\n651 \\times 300 = 651 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 1,953 \\times 100 = 195,300\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 651 by 18\n\\[\n651 \\times 18 = 651 \\times (10 + 8) = (651 \\times 10) + (651 \\times 8)\n\\]\n\\[\n651 \\times 10 = 6,510\n\\]\n\\[\n651 \\times 8 = 5,208\n\\]\n\\[\n6,510 + 5,208 = 11,718\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add the Results from Step 1 and Step 2\n\\[\n195,300 + 11,718 = 207,018\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{207,\\!018}\n\\]",
