      "text": "196,500 plus 3,275, which totals 199,775.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **655** and **305**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   655 \\times 305 = 655 \\times (300 + 5)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 655 by 300:**\n\n   \\[\n   655 \\times 300 = 655 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 1,965 \\times 100 = 196,500\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 655 by 5:**\n\n   \\[\n   655 \\times 5 = 3,275\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the two results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   196,500 + 3,275 = 199,775\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{199,\\!775}\n   \\]",
